                ============================  Mounting Volume in Linux ============================


                          - You've to create mount point means temporary directroy 

                          mkdir /mnt/sachin_lv_mount                                             Created Temp directory for mount point 

                                              |||

                          mkfs.ext4  /dev/sachin_volumegroup/sachin_lv                                      Format the disc 

                                              |||

                          mount /dev/sachin_volumegroup/sachin_lv /mnt/sachin_lv_mount                      mount to "source " to "desti"

                                              |||
 
                                            df -h                                                         mounted to  "/mnt/sachin_lv_mount"

                                              |||

                                   cd /mnt/sachin_lv_mount/                                                    Ready to use this mouted disc
 
                                               |||
                                   umount /mnt/sachin_lv_mount/                                         unmounting but data will not loss
                                                |||
                          mount /dev/sachin_volumegroup/sachin_lv /mnt/sachin_lv_mount                     Mount again


 
Note: Attaching means you're adding block to your disc , but by mount you're able to use that block


                      ============================  Managing AWS EBS on AWS EC2 Instance ===========================


